# The build context, kept to source.
#
# Without this, a Windows or macOS node_modules is copied into a Linux image --
# native modules built for the wrong platform, and a context that takes minutes
# to transfer. The Dockerfiles install their own dependencies from the lockfile,
# which is the only copy that should ever be in an image.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
.git
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log

# Nothing in the image needs these, and every one of them is a cache invalidation
# on a file that cannot affect the build.
tests
backend/tests
frontend/tests
docs
frontend/public/brand
*.md
!README.md
